<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Second Vatican Council</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1962">1962</a>–<a href="/years/1965">1965</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Vatican II</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Second Vatican Council was the 21st ecumenical council of the Catholic Church, held in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/st-peters-basilica">St. Peter's Basilica</a> from 1962 to 1965. Opened by Pope John XXIII and concluded by Paul VI, it allowed the Mass to be celebrated in local languages, recognised religious freedom, opened dialogue with other Christians and other religions, and rejected blaming the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a> collectively for the death of Christ.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/second-vatican-council.jpg" alt="Second Vatican Council" width="320" height="233" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The taker of the photo is unknown, the publisher is from Carroll College. · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vatican_II_photo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
